<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">According to Eq. <a href="#S5.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Remark 1 ‣ 5.2.2 Positive-Negative Proxy Pool ‣ 5.2 Indecisive-Categories Proxy Learning ‣ 5 Methodology ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>-<a href="#S5.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Remark 1 ‣ 5.2.2 Positive-Negative Proxy Pool ‣ 5.2 Indecisive-Categories Proxy Learning ‣ 5 Methodology ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we ensure more data participation into training while reducing potential errors of pseudo-labels. The objective of ICPL can be formulated as:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}=-\left[\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\log\frac{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{hc}}}}}{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{hc}}}}+\sum_{z_{j}\in\mathcal{R}_{i}}e^{z_{i}~\cdot~z_{j}}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ICPL</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.492em" rspace="0.492em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></msubsup></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.492em" rspace="0.492em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.492em" rspace="0.492em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}=-\left[\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\log\frac{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{hc}}}}}{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{hc}}}}+\sum_{z_{j}\in\mathcal{R}_{i}}e^{z_{i}~\cdot~z_{j}}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{lc}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{lc}}}|}\log\frac{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{lc}}}}}{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{lc}}}}+\sum_{z_{j}\in\mathcal{R}_{i}}e^{z_{i}~\cdot~z_{j}}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.492em" rspace="0.492em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lc</mtext></msubsup></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.492em" rspace="0.492em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lc</mtext></msubsup></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.492em" rspace="0.492em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{lc}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{lc}}}|}\log\frac{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{lc}}}}}{e^{z_{i}~\cdot~\omega_{i}^{\texttt{{lc}}}}+\sum_{z_{j}\in\mathcal{R}_{i}}e^{z_{i}~\cdot~z_{j}}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{lc}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">lc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{lc}}}|</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of high-confidence samples and low-confidence samples in batch <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Loss Functions</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In local training, we follow previous studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> to assign <em id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ground-truth</em> <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for labeled data and <em id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">pseudo-label</em> <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> for high-confidence unlabeled data, respectively. Following SAGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, the local losses are:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{u}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{u}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\mathbf{KL}(h_{m}(f_{m}(\mathcal{T}_{s}(\mathbf{u}_{i});\theta_{m});\omega_{m})\parallel\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">hc</mtext></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝐊𝐋</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{u}},\texttt{{hc}}}|}\mathbf{KL}(h_{m}(f_{m}(\mathcal{T}_{s}(\mathbf{u}_{i});\theta_{m});\omega_{m})\parallel\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{s}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">s</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{s}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{s}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{s}}}|}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{CE}}}(h_{m}(f_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{i};\theta_{m});\omega_{m}),\mathbf{y}_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">s</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">s</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{s}}}|}\sum_{i=1}^{|\mathcal{B}^{\texttt{{s}}}|}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{CE}}}(h_{m}(f_{m}(\mathbf{x}_{i};\theta_{m});\omega_{m}),\mathbf{y}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊𝐋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes Kullback-Leibler divergence loss, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{s}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{s}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the strong-augmentation, <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textit{{CE}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">CE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textit{{CE}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes cross-entropy loss. Following these,
our ProxyFL locally incorporate low-confidence unlabeled samples
via <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ICPL</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and improve the global category distribution via <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the server. Thus, our final total objective is:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{s}}}+\alpha\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{u}}}+\beta\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}}_{\textbf{local}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}}_{\textbf{global}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">s</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ICPL</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">local</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">global</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{s}}}+\alpha\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{u}}}+\beta\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}}_{\textbf{local}}+\underbrace{\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}}_{\textbf{global}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are empirically set to <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. The pseudo-code of ProxyFL is shown in <span id="S5.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendix. <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Pseudo-Code ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a></span>. We also provide some <span id="S5.SS3.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">theoretical proofs</span> of ProxyFL in <span id="S5.SS3.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendix. <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span> We strictly follow the FSSL experimental setting of SAGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> which is evaluated on the CIFAR10, CIFAR-100, SVHN, and CINIC-10 datasets <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>. We partition the labeled and unlabeled samples per category with label proportions of <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> for each dataset. Following previous FSSL works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, we simulate internal and external heterogeneity by sampling labeled &amp; unlabeled data from three levels of Dirichlet distribution <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Dir(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Dir(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\{0.1,0.5,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\{0.1,0.5,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and allocating them to local clients. The smaller <math id="S6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, the higher FL data heterogeneity. We visualize the specific data distribution in Fig. <a href="#S6.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 6.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>(a).</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation details</span> Following SAGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, we configure 20 clients for all settings, with 8 clients randomly sampled each round to participate in the federated training. ResNet-8 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> serves as the local backbone, with the number of local epochs set to 5, local learning rate set to 0.1 and the confidence threshold <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for pseudo-labeling set to 0.95. For global proxy tuning process, the learning rate is 0.005, and the number of tuning epochs is set to 10 for CIFAR-100 and 100 for the other datasets. Unless otherwise specified, the experimental setup of ProxyFL is consistent with SAGE (More details in Appendix. <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional Empirical Analysis ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S6.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Module ablation studies on GPT and ICPL of our method.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S6.T2.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:447.2pt;height:54.7pt;vertical-align:-25.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-75.7pt,9.3pt) scale(0.747015749117956,0.747015749117956) ;">
<table id="S6.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
