<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><math id="A2.T6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 0.97</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 1.71</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 1.60</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><math id="A2.T6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 1.18</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 0.72</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 0.84</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r"><math id="A2.T6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 0.66</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 3.29</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 2.79</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.20.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A2.T6.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;" mathcolor="#0080FF" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.T6.5.1.20.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0080FF;"> 2.69</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Theoretical Proofs</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the convergence analysis for the bi-level optimizations of ProxyFL: Global Proxy Tuning (GPT) and Indecisive-Categories Proxy Learning (ICPL). Our proofs are based on the standard assumptions in the non-convex optimization.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our GPT module is a global optimization process executed on the server. In each communication round, the server collects the local proxies <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\omega_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\omega_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> from clients and then optimizes the global proxies <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing the loss function <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. First, we give:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning)</span><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Assume that the loss function <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is L-Lipschitz and bounded below, where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is related to <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By optimizing the global proxies <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> via gradient descent with learning rate <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta_{\mathcal{G}}\leq\frac{1}{L_{\mathcal{G}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta_{\mathcal{G}}\leq\frac{1}{L_{\mathcal{G}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimization process converges to a stationary point. I.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{Q\rightarrow\infty}\frac{1}{Q}\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}\left(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}\right)\right\|^{2}\right]=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{Q\rightarrow\infty}\frac{1}{Q}\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}\left(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}\right)\right\|^{2}\right]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of proxy tuning steps on the server.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then we provide a specific proof for Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 ‣ C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. According to the descent lemma for L-smooth functions, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})+\langle\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}),\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}-\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})+\langle\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}),\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}-\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}}{2}||\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}-\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}||^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}}{2}||\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}-\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}||^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">According to the gradient-descent formula <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}=\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}-\eta_{\mathcal{G}}\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}=\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q}-\eta_{\mathcal{G}}\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})</annotation></semantics></math>, Eq. <a href="#A3.Ex5" title="In C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> can be re-written as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\eta_{\mathcal{G}}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\eta_{\mathcal{G}}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}\eta_{\mathcal{G}}^{2}}{2}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}\eta_{\mathcal{G}}^{2}}{2}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, the right side will be:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\eta_{\mathcal{G}}(1-\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}{2})||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\eta_{\mathcal{G}}(1-\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}{2})||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Let the learning rate <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathcal{G}}\leq\frac{1}{L_{\mathcal{G}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathcal{G}}\leq\frac{1}{L_{\mathcal{G}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}{2}\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{L_{\mathcal{G}}\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}{2}\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, Eq. <a href="#A3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> can be simplified to:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\frac{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}{2}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\frac{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}{2}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Rearranging the terms, we get:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}(\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}(\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Summing both the left and right sides of Eq. <a href="#A3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> from <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}(\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\underbrace{\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}(\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})-\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q+1}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}(\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{0})-\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{Q}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}(\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{0})-\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{Q}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Since we adopt InfoNCE loss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> for <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with its lowerbound <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, we thus have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})\|^{2}\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})\|^{2}\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Dividing both sides by <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the limit, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{Q\to\infty}\frac{1}{Q}\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}\leq\lim_{Q\to\infty}\frac{2\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{0})}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}Q}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">GPT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{Q\to\infty}\frac{1}{Q}\sum_{q=0}^{Q-1}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}}\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{q})||^{2}\leq\lim_{Q\to\infty}\frac{2\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{GPT}}}(\mathbf{\Omega}_{\mathcal{G}}^{0})}{\eta_{\mathcal{G}}Q}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Since the squared norm of the gradient (<em id="A3.SS1.p3.7.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e., the left-hand side of Eq. <a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a></em>) is non-negative, <span id="A3.SS1.p3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">hence we have proven Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 ‣ C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Convergence of Local Training with ICPL</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ICPL module is executed during the local training on each client. The total local loss is denoted as <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{local}}}=\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{s}}}+\alpha\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{u}}}+\beta\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">local</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">s</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">u</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ICPL</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{local}}}=\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{s}}}+\alpha\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{u}}}+\beta\mathcal{L}_{\texttt{{ICPL}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with optimization parameters <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}=\theta_{k}\cup\omega_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}=\theta_{k}\cup\omega_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Convergence of Local Training with ICPL)</span><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Suppose that the total local loss function <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for client k is L-smooth and bounded below, where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is related to <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. By optimizing the local model parameters <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> via gradient descent with learning rate <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta_{l}\leq\frac{1}{L_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta_{l}\leq\frac{1}{L_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> , the optimization
process converges to a stationary point. I.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{1}{E}\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}\mathbb{E}[||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>E</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{1}{E}\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}\mathbb{E}[||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}]=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of local training epochs.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to Sec. <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Convergence of Global Proxy Tuning ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, following the descent lemma and the gradient-descent update formula, we can similarly derive:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})-\eta_{l}(1-\frac{L_{k}\eta_{l}}{2})\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e+1})\leq\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})-\eta_{l}(1-\frac{L_{k}\eta_{l}}{2})\|\nabla_{\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By setting a local learning rate <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{l}\leq\frac{1}{L_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{l}\leq\frac{1}{L_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}||\nabla_{\Theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}||\nabla_{\Theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{l}}(\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{0})-\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{E}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{l}}(\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{0})-\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{E}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{l}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\eta_{l}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Taking the limit to Eq. <a href="#A3.Ex8" title="In C.2 Convergence of Local Training with ICPL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> and knowing that the squared norm is non-negative, we have:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{1}{E}\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\mathbf{\Theta}}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}\leq\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{2}{\eta_{l}E}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{0})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>E</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{1}{E}\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\mathbf{\Theta}}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}\leq\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{2}{\eta_{l}E}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{0})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Thus,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{1}{E}\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>E</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{E\to\infty}\frac{1}{E}\sum_{e=0}^{E-1}||\nabla_{\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}(\mathbf{\Theta}_{k}^{e})||^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">So we have proven Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 ‣ C.2 Convergence of Local Training with ICPL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Proofs ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Empirical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide some additional experiments to complement Sec. <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiments ‣ ProxyFL: A Proxy-Guided Framework for Federated Semi-Supervised Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> of our main paper, thereby offering a more robust demonstration of our proposed ProxyFL.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A4.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The communication costs per round between different methods in our experimental setting as SAGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>. <math id="A4.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> represents model parameters. <math id="A4.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.T7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the parameters after sparsely decomposition in FedMatch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, and <math id="A4.T7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> means the number of helper agents. <math id="A4.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> means respectively the number of categories and feature dimension.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A4.T7.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:472.0pt;height:292.6pt;vertical-align:-142.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(96.9pt,-60.0pt) scale(1.69614553116601,1.69614553116601) ;">
<table id="A4.T7.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
<th id="A4.T7.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Formulation</th>
<th id="A4.T7.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Practice</th></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">FixMatch+FSSL</td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="A4.T7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">22.08 M</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" rowspan="2"><span id="A4.T7.5.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text">FedMatch</span></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{M}(|\Delta\sigma_{i}|+|\Delta\psi_{i}|+C)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{M}(|\Delta\sigma_{i}|+|\Delta\psi_{i}|+C)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" rowspan="2"><span id="A4.T7.5.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text">33.12 M</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|\Delta\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}|+|\Delta\psi_{\mathcal{G}}|+H\times|\psi_{h}|))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|\Delta\sigma_{\mathcal{G}}|+|\Delta\psi_{\mathcal{G}}|+H\times|\psi_{h}|))</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">FedLabel</td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">22.08 M</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">FedDure</td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">22.08 M</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">FedDB</td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{M}(|\mathbf{\Theta}|+C)+|\mathbf{\Theta}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{M}(|\mathbf{\Theta}|+C)+|\mathbf{\Theta}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">22.08 M</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">SAGE</td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">22.08 M</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T7.5.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Proto. + FSSL</td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.T7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|+C\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m=1}^{M}|\mathbf{\Theta}|+|\mathbf{\Theta}|+C\times d</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T7.5.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">22.90 M</td></tr>
